 "description": "Mods kept on the Analog Four MKII itself (OS 1.56, core-a4mk2 0.10 or newer). It is elekloader's A4 Drive Loader (mods/drive-loader-a4mk2, vendored) under TELOS's name: a store in +Drive sectors stock never addresses (0x3000..0x7a000) holds .elemod files, sent through the unit's own Data router as /mods (Elektron Transfer, Elektroid or elekloader mods), and at every boot the ones chosen in /mods/active are linked into the +Drive mods' area, with no new firmware. SETTINGS > GLOBAL > MODS (TELOS), with TELOS's gear, opens the Drive Loader's MODS page. Hold [NO] at power-on to skip the mods once; a crash guard skips them once after a start that didn't get 10 s in. FORMAT +DRIVE empties the store.",
